{
	"name": "Faerie Firefly",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/creatures/invertebrates/fly-wasp-mosquito-green.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Resembling fireflies but in a myriad of colors, faerie fireflies often flash in shades of pink, lavender, yellow, and green. Like their cousins on the Material Plane, faerie fireflies are often found in large clusters in woodlands and fields of the faerie realms. They hold a particular affinity for invisible creatures and objects and will often flock around anything, living or not, that is unseen.</p><p>Invisible creatures and objects who are within a 10-foot radius of a cluster of faerie fireflies are under the effects of the spell @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-spells.Item.z7r6plq6vyesck07]{Faerie Fire} so long as they remain in the area of effect. Invisible creatures must succeed on a DC 15 Stealth check if they wish to pass by faerie fireflies without being detected.</p>",
